--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT SHIPPED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI FeatureFlagsPage at web parity: a pure @Observable
state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injectable
FeatureFlagsDataSource seam whose value types mirror the web FeatureFlagEntry /
FeatureFlagChange 1:1 (production binds the KMP feature-flag endpoints
GET/PUT/DELETE /system/flags* through the seam). The page reproduces the web chrome
(PageContainer title/subtitle + the "Add flag" header action) and BOTH web GlassPanels:

  GlassPanel1 — the flag registry: an adaptive key/value table (columnar Grid on
    macOS/iPad, per-row cards on iPhone) sorted by key ascending, with the web
    previewValue JSON preview and per-row Edit + Delete actions.
  GlassPanel2 — the recent change-audit feed: an adaptive 7-column table (Changed at,
    Actor, Key, Operation badge, Old, New, Reason) with the web `compact` JSON preview
    and the set→success / delete→danger operation badge.

The create/edit drawer (web FlagEditDrawer) and the delete confirmation (web Modal)
are presented as HIG-native sheets sharing a FeatureFlagSheetScaffold: the editor is a
free-form JSON editor (invalid JSON disables Save + surfaces the inline parse error,
the reason is required), and the delete dialog confirms a permanent removal with a
required reason and cannot be dismissed mid-flight. Arbitrary JSON flag values are
modelled by FlagJSONValue (parse / pretty / compact / preview ported from the web).

Files (all new unless noted):
  Sources/Features/Admin/FeatureFlagJSON.swift              (FlagJSONValue)
  Sources/Features/Admin/FeatureFlagsModels.swift          (entry/change/op/states/datasource/format)
  Sources/Features/Admin/FeatureFlagsPageModel.swift       (@Observable model)
  Sources/Features/Admin/FeatureFlagsPageModel.Sample.swift(actor seed source)
  Sources/Features/Admin/FeatureFlagsPage.swift            (view: header + 2 panels + sheets)
  Sources/Features/Admin/FeatureFlagsPage.Table.swift      (registry table)
  Sources/Features/Admin/FeatureFlagsPage.Changes.swift    (changes table + op badge)
  Sources/Features/Admin/FeatureFlagsPage.Editor.swift     (editor sheet + scaffold)
  Sources/Features/Admin/FeatureFlagsPage.Delete.swift     (delete sheet)
  Sources/Features/Admin/FeatureFlagsRouteRegistration.swift(.featureFlags route)
  Tests/Unit/Features/Admin/FeatureFlagsPageModelTests.swift(state-machine + value tests)
  Sources/App/AppRoute.swift            (MOD: +.featureFlags case / pathSegment / icon / group)
  Sources/App/AppRouteParser.swift      (MOD: +"/admin/flags" -> .featureFlags alias)
  Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift            (MOD: wire FeatureFlagsRouteRegistration into routeHosts)
  Localization/Localizable.xcstrings    (MOD: +40 keys incl. route.featureFlags)
  apps/parity/apple-ledger.json         (MOD: +2 rows page:admin/FeatureFlags 16/16)

Navigation reconciliation: web /admin/flags resolves to a dedicated .featureFlags
route (pathSegment "feature-flags", System sidebar group) via an AppRouteParser alias,
mirroring the sibling .auditLog (/admin/audit-log) pattern — reachable + deep-linkable
without displacing other admin pages. The generated TeslaSync.xcodeproj is git-ignored.

